# Environment
# .env holds placeholder values committed for CI asset bundling (see CLAUDE.md).
# Real/local overrides go in .env.local, which stays ignored.
.env.local

# Stray env fragment (no secrets — documentation snippet)
.github/.env

.claude/

# Android release signing — credentials and keystores are never committed
# (LOCKED PRINCIPLE #6). Create android/key.properties locally from the
# founder-issued keystore; see docs/BETA_ROLLBACK.md.
android/key.properties
*.keystore
*.jks

# Sentry symbol-upload credentials: auth token, org and project live ONLY in
# the shell environment or an untracked sentry.properties. Never committed.
sentry.properties
android/sentry.properties
ios/sentry.properties

# Private registry exports — never committed.
#
# This is prospective protection against accidentally recommitting a private
# NHFR export. It is NOT breach remediation: no personal-data breach was
# established, and no such file has ever been committed to this repository.
#
# The NHFR export is withheld because its redistribution terms were never
# captured — the registry publishes no licence and reserves all rights. It is
# also large enough to bloat every clone (~20 MB).
#
# Licensed public datasets are a different matter and MAY remain tracked
# wherever their attribution and redistribution requirements are satisfied —
# GRID3 (CC BY 4.0) and HOTOSM/OpenStreetMap (ODbL) among them. The negations
# below keep this rule from ever blocking one.
#
# Keep private exports outside Git entirely and pass the path to the audit
# scripts, either as an argument or through WELLAPATH_PRIVATE_DATA. Only
# derived, contact-free, aggregate artifacts belong in the repository.
nigeria_health_facilities.csv
nhfr_*.csv
facilities_export_*.csv

# Licensed public sources are never caught by the rules above.
!grid3_*.csv
!GRID3_*.csv
!hotosm_*.csv
!HOTOSM_*.csv
